Bug 318600 - Implement text background colour in mail editor.

Patch summary: Text background colour selector in the compose window

- editFormatButtons.inc.xhtml
  - Added TextBackgroundColorButton to the ColorButtons stack (calls
    EditorSelectColor('TextBackground', event), observes cmd_highlight).
  - BackgroundColorButton tooltip migrated from DTD to Fluent
    (compose-tool-button-page-background-color).
- editor.js
  - EditorSelectColor('TextBackground') reuses the existing Highlight/backColor
    machinery; applies execCommand("backColor") and updates the button
    immediately after picking (pending styles are not in the DOM until typing).
  - GetTextBackgroundColorState(): reads bgcolor/inline background-color from
    the selection (the mail editor reports transparent for cmd_highlight);
    collapsed caret -> colour at caret; non-collapsed -> walks the selected
    text runs and returns "mixed" when colours differ (correct boundary
    handling).
  - SetTextBackgroundColorButton(): sets swatch colour, transparent when none,
    multicolor icon for mixed.
- ComposerCommands.js
  - pokeMultiStateUI refreshes the text bg button on every cmd_highlight update
    (selection-change feedback), since the editor state never changes from
    transparent.
- messengercompose.css
  - Three-button stack layout: page background fills the stack, text bg
    bottom-right, text colour top-left.
  - Empty state shows a cross (X) via GrayText gradients; mixed state shows
    multicolor.png.
- messengercompose.ftl
  - New compose-tool-button-text-background-color ("Choose color for text
    background") and compose-tool-button-page-background-color ("Choose color
    for page background").
- editorOverlay.dtd
  - Removed BackgroundColorButton.tooltip.
- dialogs/EdColorPicker.xhtml
  - Added LastHighlightColor to the persisted attributes, so the panel offers
    the last-picked text background colour across compose windows/sessions.

